au_test*/
sanity_dry/
logs/

# The retrieved documents never ship: 19 GB across six economies, regenerated by
# `crawl`, and every one of them is a public law still on its portal. The root
# .gitignore already excludes `raw/` at every depth; this repeats it beside the
# code it applies to, and adds the two folder names China uses instead — its
# layer-2 collector writes document bodies to `files/` and extracted plain text to
# `text/`, so a rule that names only `raw/` lets 8.7 MB of retrieved law through.
handoff1/**/raw/
handoff1/**/files/
handoff1/**/text/
handoff1/**/*.pdf
handoff1/**/*.doc
handoff1/**/*.docx
handoff1/**/*.zip

# What DOES ship, deliberately: handoff1/ itself. Each economy's corpus keeps its
# manifest, law table, link records, audit and note — about 68 MB that describes
# every document without containing one, so a reviewer can check a flagged row and
# verify a provenance claim without the 19 GB. See handoff1/README.md.
#
# The Round 1 hand-off (handoff1_v2/) and the prior-generation scraper (File_2025/)
# are not in this tree at all, so the rules that used to protect them are gone.
